[chuckles] That's understandable.

256
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:36,329
It's okay.

257
00:16:37,038 --> 00:16:37,872
Let's go.

258
00:16:39,541 --> 00:16:41,876
Hello. Welcome. Which one's a good flavor?

259
00:16:42,419 --> 00:16:43,877
Well, right now we have

260
00:16:43,878 --> 00:16:45,587
the almond and caramel bonbons.

261
00:16:45,588 --> 00:16:47,840
These are selling really well
at the moment.

262
00:16:47,841 --> 00:16:49,509
They're our newest flavor. Yum.

263
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:54,346
So there's this really fun one
we've called Rainbow Watermelon.

264
00:16:54,347 --> 00:16:56,390
This one's also a new flavor,

265
00:16:56,391 --> 00:16:58,560
so a lot of customers
are currently trying it.

266
00:16:59,269 --> 00:17:00,936
[man] Cool. I like those sweet flavors.

267
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:02,813
But if you prefer
an even sweeter option...

268
00:17:02,814 --> 00:17:04,648
- Yeah.
- ...then I recommend my favorite,

269
00:17:04,649 --> 00:17:06,609
which is the Giant Chocolate Puzzle.

270
00:17:07,068 --> 00:17:08,360
- You should try it.
- [man] Okay.

271
00:17:08,361 --> 00:17:09,696
That's the one we make...

272
00:17:11,698 --> 00:17:14,074
So are you dating Young-joo or--

273
00:17:14,075 --> 00:17:16,828
What are you saying? No way, dude!
It's not like that.

274
00:17:17,871 --> 00:17:18,705
Really?

275
00:17:19,873 --> 00:17:21,916
There's still a chance. [laughs]

276
00:17:23,877 --> 00:17:25,086
[laughs]

277
00:17:28,423 --> 00:17:29,257
Hey...

278
00:17:30,175 --> 00:17:31,967
not to be rude, however,

279
00:17:31,968 --> 00:17:34,678
are you really in a position
to turn her down, like--

280
00:17:34,679 --> 00:17:37,515
There you go talking weird again
Seriously, stop it.

281
00:17:38,892 --> 00:17:40,518
It was just a question. My bad.

282
00:17:41,186 --> 00:17:42,020
Ugh!

283
00:17:44,397 --> 00:17:46,565
Well, you aren't completely wrong,
you know.

284
00:17:46,566 --> 00:17:47,484
Huh?

285
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:49,943
[sighs]

286
00:17:49,944 --> 00:17:53,281
In what scenario would a girl like her
date me, really?

287
00:17:53,990 --> 00:17:55,408
Impossible. Huh?

288
00:17:55,992 --> 00:17:57,451
- Right?
- [sighs]

289
00:17:57,452 --> 00:17:59,871
- [sobbing]
- [man] Hey!

290
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:02,456
Why are you crying?

291
00:18:02,457 --> 00:18:04,249
[manager] Young-joo, are you okay?

292
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:06,001
- I'm okay. [sobbing]
- What--

293
00:18:06,002 --> 00:18:09,214
All I did was ask
for an almond caramel bonbon.

294
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:12,509
No, no, no. It really isn't your fault.

295
00:18:13,468 --> 00:18:16,637
Sir, I'm really not feeling well.
May I be excused?

296
00:18:16,638 --> 00:18:18,472
[manager] Oh, yes. Please go home.

297
00:18:18,473 --> 00:18:20,974
[sobbing]

298
00:18:20,975 --> 00:18:23,435
Young-joo, it's okay. We'll handle it.

299
00:18:23,436 --> 00:18:24,478
Young-joo, I--

300
00:18:24,479 --> 00:18:25,396
[bell dings]

301
00:18:35,949 --> 00:18:37,951
[engine whirring]

302
00:18:39,369 --> 00:18:41,371
[sniffling, sobbing]

303
00:18:43,581 --> 00:18:45,625
Shit! This sucks.

304
00:18:46,292 --> 00:18:47,377
Oh, so embarrassing.

305
00:18:48,378 --> 00:18:50,380
[crying]

306
00:19:05,353 --> 00:19:07,146
Young-joo, I was actually thinking...

307
00:19:08,731 --> 00:19:11,024
- about what I said earlier.
- God damn it!

308
00:19:11,025 --> 00:19:12,026
Hey, hold on!

309
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:14,444
Hey, Young-joo, hold on.

310
00:19:14,445 --> 00:19:15,989
- [screams]
- Hey! Whoa, whoa!

311
00:19:17,031 --> 00:19:19,951
- [cries] It's so freaking annoying.
- You okay?

312
00:19:20,535 --> 00:19:23,662
- Young-joo.
- It's always getting undone! [cries]

313
00:19:23,663 --> 00:19:24,581
Wait, what?

314
00:19:25,456 --> 00:19:28,501
God damn it! This freaking shoelace
is always undone!

315
00:19:29,210 --> 00:19:30,044
The shoelace?

316
00:19:33,256 --> 00:19:35,550
You should have told me.
I could have taught you.

317
00:19:36,342 --> 00:19:39,095
I'm actually quite skilled
in tying shoelaces.

318
00:19:41,681 --> 00:19:42,515
Really?

319
00:19:44,309 --> 00:19:46,436
[Jae-yoon] Of course.
Look, just like this.

320
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:50,106
This goes through here...

321
00:19:51,357 --> 00:19:52,191
and then...

322
00:19:54,903 --> 00:19:57,071
Am I really that bad?

323
00:19:59,407 --> 00:20:00,241
[Jae-yoon] Not bad.

324
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:04,245
You're beautiful.

325
00:20:13,004 --> 00:20:16,799
Hey, Jae-yoon, you asshole!
It did come undone.

326
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:20,678
You're very relaxed, huh?

327
00:20:21,471 --> 00:20:23,806
Young-joo, please, just get
it together and hurry up!

328
00:20:28,519 --> 00:20:30,521
[panting]

329
00:20:32,565 --> 00:20:33,941
Lee Jae-yoon and In-ho.

330
00:20:33,942 --> 00:20:36,151
- Yes, sir.
- Private Ra In-ho.

331
00:20:36,152 --> 00:20:37,070
What can we do?

332
00:20:38,321 --> 00:20:39,197
It's over, right?

333
00:20:42,659 --> 00:20:43,784
[gasps]

334
00:20:43,785 --> 00:20:46,536
[growling]

335
00:20:46,537 --> 00:20:48,414
[both exclaim]

336
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:55,630
[exclaiming]

337
00:21:02,011 --> 00:21:04,347
- What the fuck?
- Get it together!

338
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:06,641
Fuck! Fuck!

339
00:21:08,017 --> 00:21:11,228
What the fuck is that thing?

340
00:21:11,229 --> 00:21:13,314
[snarling]

341
00:21:17,568 --> 00:21:18,403
[guns cocking]

342
00:21:22,573 --> 00:21:23,449
What do we do?

343
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:25,450
[Jae-yoon] Get back!

344
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:26,869
[exclaiming]

345
00:21:30,665 --> 00:21:32,458
- [snarling]
- [screaming]

346
00:21:38,006 --> 00:21:39,298
- Ahh!
- [snarls]

347
00:21:39,757 --> 00:21:41,508
- [In-ho] Corporal Jeon Hyung-bae!
- [clangs]

348
00:21:41,509 --> 00:21:43,177
- [snarling]
- [screaming]

349
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:45,596
Kim Young-man, shoot!

350
00:21:46,848 --> 00:21:47,682
[grunts]

351
00:21:48,558 --> 00:21:50,517
[screaming]

352
00:21:50,518 --> 00:21:52,603
[clanging]

353
00:21:55,898 --> 00:21:57,066
[Tae-hwa] Shoot it now!

354
00:21:59,652 --> 00:22:00,611
I'm so sorry for this.

355
00:22:03,698 --> 00:22:04,532
[gunshot]

356
00:22:06,701 --> 00:22:07,952
Quickly. Let's go.

357
00:22:10,747 --> 00:22:12,290
[exclaims]

358
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:15,084
God damn it.

359
00:22:16,419 --> 00:22:17,962
Are you okay?

360
00:22:19,380 --> 00:22:20,214
[Jin-wook] Look.

361
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,342
Please, help me.

362
00:22:25,386 --> 00:22:28,139
No, no, no! No! No! I'm not infected.

363
00:22:29,891 --> 00:22:30,850
Wait, hold up!

364
00:22:31,517 --> 00:22:33,435
If he can talk, then maybe it's true.

365
00:22:33,436 --> 00:22:34,728
Let's not kill him yet.

366
00:22:34,729 --> 00:22:35,980
[man] Fucking hell!

367
00:22:36,689 --> 00:22:38,232
If you wanna kill me, do it.

368
00:22:39,067 --> 00:22:41,568
Did you get bitten by a zombie?

369
00:22:41,569 --> 00:22:43,820
- I got bitten, man.
- [Tae-shik] Hey!

370
00:22:43,821 --> 00:22:45,907
I got bitten and that's why
I have this shit.

371
00:22:46,657 --> 00:22:49,077
On top of that,
you're all trying to smack me?

372
00:22:49,619 --> 00:22:50,745
That's mean, dude.

373
00:22:51,579 --> 00:22:54,582
Just go.
You're all just a bunch of assholes.

374
00:22:56,876 --> 00:22:58,336
Go fuck yourselves!

375
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:03,508
Look, he's slurring his words.
He's too far gone to be a zombie.

376
00:23:04,175 --> 00:23:05,593
- Let's go now.
- Let's go now.

377
00:23:06,344 --> 00:23:09,639
Hey, are you guys really
gonna leave me here?

378
00:23:10,807 --> 00:23:12,599
Help me! Help me!

379
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:14,018
I don't wanna die.

380
00:23:16,437 --> 00:23:18,481
Oh, a Yoon Jong-shin fanatic.

381
00:23:19,148 --> 00:23:20,691
- Please, help me.
- What?

382
00:23:21,567 --> 00:23:22,692
Can't he come with us?

383
00:23:22,693 --> 00:23:24,903
- No way!
- I'm begging you to save me.

384
00:23:24,904 --> 00:23:26,947
- Please. Just this once.
- Does it really hurt?

385
00:23:26,948 --> 00:23:28,615
Have you gone completely insane?

386
00:23:28,616 --> 00:23:30,284
If you're too scared then go!

387
00:23:30,785 --> 00:23:33,370
You serious?
Why are you talking to me like that?

388
00:23:33,371 --> 00:23:35,288
You said I could be less formal
when eating.

389
00:23:35,289 --> 00:23:36,665
So that's me being casual.

390
00:23:36,666 --> 00:23:38,751
You don't like it?
Then leave, Seo Jin-wook.

391
00:23:39,877 --> 00:23:41,086
[mobile ringing]

392
00:23:41,087 --> 00:23:43,296
Hang up! Hang up!

393
00:23:43,297 --> 00:23:46,342
- Turn it off! Where is it?
- [grunting]

394
00:23:51,889 --> 00:23:55,475
- Yoon Jong-shin!
- Sorry. I was supposed to be studying--

395
00:23:55,476 --> 00:23:56,893
- [all] Shh!
- [snarling]

396
00:23:56,894 --> 00:23:58,813
Ah, shit! I told you to leave the guy.

397
00:23:59,313 --> 00:24:01,439
This way. Let's get out of here!

398
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,109
- [man] Let's go!
- [Young-joo screams]

399
00:24:03,651 --> 00:24:04,485
[Tae-shik] This way!

400
00:24:05,486 --> 00:24:07,488
- [snarling]
- [screaming]

401
00:24:09,657 --> 00:24:11,366
[snarling]

402
00:24:11,367 --> 00:24:14,077
- [gunshot]
- Ahh! [pants]

403
00:24:14,078 --> 00:24:15,163
[thuds]

404
00:24:19,167 --> 00:24:20,293
[Gye-young] Soo-jeong.

405
00:24:27,592 --> 00:24:28,426
Hyung-bae.

406
00:24:30,052 --> 00:24:31,053
[whimpers]

407
00:24:31,721 --> 00:24:33,347
What were you thinking shooting a gun?

408
00:24:33,890 --> 00:24:35,391
It's reckless and it's prohibited!

409
00:24:36,726 --> 00:24:37,560
I'm sorry...

410
00:24:38,686 --> 00:24:39,854
- Apologies.
- Sir!

411
00:24:41,439 --> 00:24:43,648
If Soo-jeong hadn't acted,
In-Ho would have died.

412
00:24:43,649 --> 00:24:45,318
Kwak Gye-young, know your damn place!

413
00:24:49,822 --> 00:24:51,199
You all get your shit together!

414
00:24:53,534 --> 00:24:54,619
- Kwak Gye-young.
- Sir.

415
00:24:55,119 --> 00:24:56,746
Take her to the living quarters.

416
00:24:57,413 --> 00:24:58,581
Take care of Hyung-bae.

417
00:25:00,124 --> 00:25:01,751
Remove the bodies immediately.

418
00:25:03,628 --> 00:25:05,462
- Get to it!
- Yes, sir.

419
00:25:05,463 --> 00:25:06,380
[all] Yes, sir.

420
00:25:08,591 --> 00:25:10,091
- Come on.
- Come on.

421
00:25:10,092 --> 00:25:11,384
Please take this.

422
00:25:11,385 --> 00:25:13,095
- Commander...
- It's safer inside.

423
00:25:13,846 --> 00:25:15,598
Park Sung-wook, are you listening to me?

424
00:25:16,974 --> 00:25:19,185
- Yeah.
- I'll report this to the brigade.

425
00:25:20,269 --> 00:25:22,021
Get your shit together, Commander.

426
00:25:24,273 --> 00:25:25,358
Yes. Thanks you're right.

427
00:25:28,194 --> 00:25:30,071
I think I'll rest inside for a while.

428
00:25:34,408 --> 00:25:35,243
[coughing]

429
00:25:36,827 --> 00:25:37,662
Cover him.

430
00:25:39,914 --> 00:25:41,916
[snarling]

431
00:25:46,587 --> 00:25:48,714
[Young-joo] Oh.
They're really going at it.

432
00:25:49,298 --> 00:25:50,132
Hold up. Go in.

433
00:25:55,096 --> 00:25:56,514
Hey, I'm sorry.

434
00:25:57,974 --> 00:25:59,892
But if you wanna join us,
we have no choice

435
00:26:00,017 --> 00:26:01,226
...but to tie you up.

436
00:26:01,227 --> 00:26:02,478
If he makes it.

437
00:26:03,104 --> 00:26:04,354
Makes it?

438
00:26:04,355 --> 00:26:06,523
If he can make it any longer, you know?

439
00:26:06,524 --> 00:26:09,235
Look how his eyes are getting red.
He's transforming.

440
00:26:09,902 --> 00:26:11,279
[mumbling]

441
00:26:13,281 --> 00:26:14,489
Any ideas on what to do?

442
00:26:14,490 --> 00:26:16,950
- Murder him?
- [mumbling and whimpering]

443
00:26:16,951 --> 00:26:19,244
He's gonna turn into a zombie right now!

444
00:26:19,245 --> 00:26:20,830
[mumbling and whimpering]

445
00:26:22,498 --> 00:26:24,666
Oh, you want us to pity you, you asshole?

446
00:26:24,667 --> 00:26:27,168
[sighs] That's why I tied up
his mouth and his hands.

447
00:26:27,169 --> 00:26:29,212
Young-joo, don't pretend to be nice.

448
00:26:29,213 --> 00:26:30,672
- I mean, seriously.
- Jin-wook!

449
00:26:30,673 --> 00:26:33,592
- [Tripeater mumbling]
- "Don't pretend"? That's a little harsh.

450
00:26:33,718 --> 00:26:36,344
- Huh? Then what should I say? "Fuck"?
- [Tripeater sobbing]

451
00:26:36,345 --> 00:26:39,681
Let me tell you, if it weren't for her,
none of this would be h--

452
00:26:39,682 --> 00:26:41,308
- Hey!
- [Tae-shik] Relax, man.

453
00:26:41,309 --> 00:26:43,560
Young-joo, you need to stop this now.

454
00:26:43,561 --> 00:26:45,562
- Okay?
- You son of a bitch! What's your deal?

455
00:26:45,563 --> 00:26:47,897
- I'll smash your face in, you zombie!
- [Tae-shik] Stop.

456
00:26:47,898 --> 00:26:49,482
- Son of a-- [grunts]
- [vomits]

457
00:26:49,483 --> 00:26:50,943
[gagging]

458
00:26:52,069 --> 00:26:53,153
[Jin-wook grunts]

459
00:26:53,154 --> 00:26:55,363
- [Young-joo groans]
- Let's untie him. Yeah?

460
00:26:55,364 --> 00:26:57,741
If something happens,
it's not my fault, okay?

461
00:26:57,742 --> 00:26:59,701
[gagging]

462
00:26:59,702 --> 00:27:01,412
- [vomiting]
- [all groaning]

463
00:27:03,039 --> 00:27:05,123
[Young-joo] Dude, how much did you drink?

464
00:27:05,124 --> 00:27:06,542
[Tripeater inhales deeply]

465
00:27:07,043 --> 00:27:10,295
There was the Chinese restaurant.

466
00:27:10,296 --> 00:27:12,547
<i>- Two bottles of</i> soju.
- [sighs]

467
00:27:12,548 --> 00:27:16,218
And then there's
the bottles at Hangang Park.

468
00:27:17,636 --> 00:27:19,763
- [sighs]
- And then...

469
00:27:19,764 --> 00:27:21,222
<i>another bottle</i>

470
00:27:21,223 --> 00:27:24,560
<i>- at the restaurant for the hangover.</i>
- What the hell?

471
00:27:26,145 --> 00:27:28,939
- [zombie snarling and growling]
- [screaming]

472
00:27:30,900 --> 00:27:32,108
<i>I had something else.</i>

473
00:27:32,109 --> 00:27:33,443
What did I eat?

474
00:27:33,444 --> 00:27:35,320
Just look down and you'll find out.

475
00:27:35,321 --> 00:27:37,280
You ate some fried rice.

476
00:27:37,281 --> 00:27:39,075
Water. Water, please, guys.

477
00:27:39,700 --> 00:27:43,495
[chuckles] You failed finals three times
and went drinking instead of studying?

478
00:27:43,496 --> 00:27:45,414
- Are you going for a fourth time?
- Whoa.

479
00:27:46,290 --> 00:27:48,041
A fourth time?

480
00:27:48,042 --> 00:27:50,126
Don't you dare say such horrible things.

481
00:27:50,127 --> 00:27:53,589
If I fail a fourth time,
I'll have to join the army.

482
00:27:54,632 --> 00:27:56,341
I had a drink to take the edge off.

483
00:27:56,342 --> 00:27:57,760
- That's all.
- [Young-joo sighs]

484
00:28:00,429 --> 00:28:01,389
Bring the water.

485
00:28:01,972 --> 00:28:03,640
- [Tripeater] Water.
- Wait, me?

486
00:28:03,641 --> 00:28:04,682
Come on. Go get it.

487
00:28:04,683 --> 00:28:07,060
[sighs] Sure thing. Anything at all.

488
00:28:07,061 --> 00:28:09,772
- Why don't you give him one more drink?
- If I may interject...

489
00:28:11,399 --> 00:28:13,358
I might have a couple theories.

490
00:28:13,359 --> 00:28:15,235
- [Young-joo screams]
- [zombie growling]

491
00:28:15,236 --> 00:28:17,654
[Young-joo and Tripeater screaming]

492
00:28:17,655 --> 00:28:20,698
- [gasps and whimpers]
- [Young-joo groans]

493
00:28:20,699 --> 00:28:22,618
- [zombie snarling]
- [gasps]

494
00:28:23,494 --> 00:28:25,663
- [zombie snarling]
- [yelling]

495
00:28:26,789 --> 00:28:29,917
- [zombie snarling]
- [Young-joo yelling]

496
00:28:32,378 --> 00:28:34,046
- [thuds]
- [zombie snarling]

497
00:28:35,714 --> 00:28:36,548
[splattering]

498
00:28:36,549 --> 00:28:38,926
[whimpering]

499
00:28:43,681 --> 00:28:46,099
- [gasps]
- Wait, wait, wait.

500
00:28:46,100 --> 00:28:47,935
[quirky music playing]

501
00:28:48,894 --> 00:28:51,480
{\an8}- [blows air]
- [breathalyzer beeping]

502
00:28:55,609 --> 00:28:57,987
[breathalyzer beeping]

503
00:28:59,447 --> 00:29:01,906
- Fuck yeah!
- [Jin-wook] Jesus! He scared me.

504
00:29:01,907 --> 00:29:03,116
What's wrong with him?

505
00:29:03,117 --> 00:29:04,784
[panicked screaming]

506
00:29:04,785 --> 00:29:06,661
[Tae-shik] Ta-da! Look at this.

507
00:29:06,662 --> 00:29:09,205
- He's drunk. So what?
- You saw it, right?

508
00:29:09,206 --> 00:29:11,291
You saw how that thing ran past the guy.

509
00:29:11,292 --> 00:29:14,002
Uh, yeah, I think I did.

510
00:29:14,003 --> 00:29:15,211
There were a bunch of them.

511
00:29:15,212 --> 00:29:18,047
They went right past that guy
and ran directly for us.

512
00:29:18,048 --> 00:29:20,341
Can you please
just cut to the chase and explain?

513
00:29:20,342 --> 00:29:21,885
I've come to two theories.

514
00:29:21,886 --> 00:29:25,221
One, if you've had a lot to drink,
the zombies won't attack you.

515
00:29:25,222 --> 00:29:26,681
Two, even when bitten,

516
00:29:26,682 --> 00:29:28,767
if you're drunk,
you don't turn into a zombie.

517
00:29:30,352 --> 00:29:33,021
So, I think getting wasted
is our best option.

518
00:29:33,022 --> 00:29:34,690
- [chuckles] Well...
- Wasted?

519
00:29:35,316 --> 00:29:37,609
- For Christ's sake.
- [Young-joo] That sounds dumb.

520
00:29:37,610 --> 00:29:39,653
Then how do you explain this guy, huh?

521
00:29:40,779 --> 00:29:43,239
It's just a theory,
but what else have we got?

522
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:45,951
- [panicked screaming]
- We should start drinking now.

523
00:29:46,535 --> 00:29:48,621
- What?
- How much should we drink?

524
00:29:49,830 --> 00:29:51,206
- [Tae-shik] This much.
- [gasps]

525
00:29:51,207 --> 00:29:52,541
[Jin-wook] Wow. That's...

526
00:29:53,626 --> 00:29:54,752
How you end up like that?

527
00:29:55,628 --> 00:29:58,296
Why are you looking at me?
I'm so offended.

528
00:29:58,297 --> 00:30:00,298
I'm a drunk too, and I admit it.

529
00:30:00,299 --> 00:30:03,968
I'd rather go out when it's light out,
So let's drink till morning.

530
00:30:03,969 --> 00:30:06,846
Okay? Let's drink.

531
00:30:06,847 --> 00:30:08,389
[Jin-wook] Let's drink.

532
00:30:08,390 --> 00:30:11,226
[Tripeater] Will you give me
a bottle too, right?

533
00:30:11,227 --> 00:30:13,269
Please? Please, I...

534
00:30:13,270 --> 00:30:14,521
- Shit.
- [line ringing]

535
00:30:14,522 --> 00:30:16,190
[Tripeater] I wanna drink too.

536
00:30:17,650 --> 00:30:18,691
[Tripeater moans]

537
00:30:18,692 --> 00:30:19,985
[automated voice] <i>I'm sorry.</i>

538
00:30:20,486 --> 00:30:23,530
<i>- The number you are trying to reach...</i>
- [Tripeater] So thirsty.

539
00:30:23,531 --> 00:30:24,739
JAE-YOON

540
00:30:24,740 --> 00:30:26,324
[Young-joo] <i>Jae-yoon,</i>

541
00:30:26,325 --> 00:30:29,661
<i>I'm hiding in a restaurant
that's very close to Tower A.</i>

542
00:30:29,662 --> 00:30:31,872
{\an8}<i>If you see this, please call me.</i>

543
00:30:32,790 --> 00:30:34,040
[mellow music playing]

544
00:30:34,041 --> 00:30:35,417
[Tae-shik] Ta-da. Bottoms up.

545
00:30:38,379 --> 00:30:40,923
- [sighs]
- [Tripeater] Sir, I'd like one too.

546
00:30:42,633 --> 00:30:43,551
Sir?

547
00:30:47,471 --> 00:30:49,098
[friend 1] Don't cry, Young-joo.

548
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:50,766
Thanks for being here.

549
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:52,267
Please, eat.

550
00:30:52,268 --> 00:30:53,769
[indistinct chatter]

551
00:30:55,104 --> 00:30:58,065
- [friend 2] You should eat too.
- [Young-joo] I'm not hungry.

552
00:31:02,903 --> 00:31:05,029
- [Jae-yoon] Are you crying?
- Oh, my God. [chuckles]

553
00:31:05,030 --> 00:31:06,906
- [Jae-yoon chuckles]
- I'm not.

554
00:31:06,907 --> 00:31:08,950
- Smile. Come on, smile.
- Hey! [chuckles]

555
00:31:08,951 --> 00:31:10,411
Seriously. [chuckles]

556
00:31:11,203 --> 00:31:13,163
- Aren't you tired?
- Not at all.

557
00:31:13,664 --> 00:31:16,666
- I want to say thank you.
- No need. I'll always be here.

558
00:31:16,667 --> 00:31:18,586
[music continues playing]

559
00:31:21,297 --> 00:31:23,007
A present from my father.

560
00:31:25,551 --> 00:31:26,552
[sighs]

561
00:31:29,513 --> 00:31:31,765
He really didn't have
to leave me anything.

562
00:31:33,559 --> 00:31:36,103
- [chuckles] Thank you, sir.
- [chuckles]

563
00:31:38,689 --> 00:31:40,815
I thought you knew I didn't smoke though.

564
00:31:40,816 --> 00:31:42,775
- [chuckles]
- Huh?

565
00:31:42,776 --> 00:31:45,696
- Hey, my dad didn't smoke either.
- [chuckles]

566
00:31:47,114 --> 00:31:48,157
That's true.

567
00:31:49,867 --> 00:31:51,701
Hey, I saw him carrying this around,

568
00:31:51,702 --> 00:31:54,204
but I never actually saw him
smoking a cigarette.

569
00:31:55,289 --> 00:31:56,290
This is...

570
00:31:57,041 --> 00:32:00,127
what I gifted my dad when I was younger
using my allowance.

571
00:32:01,253 --> 00:32:05,466
Since then, he always carried it around,
protecting it like some prized possession.

572
00:32:06,425 --> 00:32:09,177
Whenever he'd see me,
he'd pretend to smoke a cigarette.

573
00:32:09,178 --> 00:32:11,221
[chuckles] It always brightened my day.

574
00:32:13,098 --> 00:32:14,558
[chuckles and sniffles]

575
00:32:19,647 --> 00:32:20,521
[sucks]

576
00:32:20,522 --> 00:32:21,774
[inhales through mouth]

577
00:32:22,524 --> 00:32:23,692
- [blows air]
- [chuckles]

578
00:32:24,693 --> 00:32:26,110
Stop that. [chuckles]

579
00:32:26,111 --> 00:32:28,071
- What a smoke. So good.
- Cut it out.

580
00:32:28,072 --> 00:32:29,198
[gasps]

581
00:32:32,660 --> 00:32:33,661
Young-joo.

582
00:32:42,002 --> 00:32:42,920
[groans softly]

583
00:32:47,049 --> 00:32:47,966
[sighs]

584
00:32:52,638 --> 00:32:53,971
[slow music playing]

585
00:32:53,972 --> 00:32:56,392
NAME: LEE JAE-YOON
POSITION: SHINGUNG ASSISTANT

586
00:32:58,727 --> 00:32:59,645
[sighs]

587
00:33:14,451 --> 00:33:15,994
[siren wailing distantly]

588
00:33:29,299 --> 00:33:30,134
[sniffles]

589
00:33:31,719 --> 00:33:32,803
[tapping keys]

590
00:33:33,971 --> 00:33:35,264
[line ringing]

591
00:33:37,975 --> 00:33:39,727
- [line disconnects]
- [sighs]

592
00:33:40,644 --> 00:33:41,811
YOUNG-JOO, MY LOVE

593
00:33:41,812 --> 00:33:42,730
[sighs]

594
00:33:44,148 --> 00:33:44,982
[softly] Fuck.

595
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:48,944
[sighs]

596
00:33:49,820 --> 00:33:51,571
[Sung-wook panting]

597
00:33:51,572 --> 00:33:53,157
[solemn music playing]

598
00:33:55,784 --> 00:33:56,702
Oh, shit.

599
00:33:57,494 --> 00:33:58,620
[panting]

600
00:34:05,377 --> 00:34:06,211
[grunts]

601
00:34:06,795 --> 00:34:08,172
[breath trembling]

602
00:34:16,513 --> 00:34:17,931
[breath trembling]

603
00:34:20,851 --> 00:34:22,227
[sobbing]

604
00:34:22,770 --> 00:34:23,895
Oh, shit.

605
00:34:23,896 --> 00:34:25,397
[sobbing]

606
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:49,212
[Seon-mi] <i>The country
is in a state of turmoil today</i>

607
00:34:49,213 --> 00:34:52,131
<i>as continued attacks
have left the population anxious</i>

608
00:34:52,132 --> 00:34:53,634
<i>and fearful for their lives.</i>

609
00:34:54,343 --> 00:34:55,551
<i>What we know so far</i>

610
00:34:55,552 --> 00:34:58,513
<i>is that these zombie perpetrators
assault indiscriminately</i>

611
00:34:58,514 --> 00:35:00,057
<i>for no known reason.</i>

612
00:35:00,724 --> 00:35:03,893
<i>The monsters have been witnessed
striking victims from all directions,</i>

613
00:35:03,894 --> 00:35:06,103
<i>killing them
through bites to their bodies.</i>

614
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:09,440
<i>The government has suspended
all public transportation,</i>

615
00:35:09,441 --> 00:35:11,692
<i>including subways and busses.</i>

616
00:35:11,693 --> 00:35:14,070
{\an8}<i>It is imperative for the safety
of the general public</i>

617
00:35:14,071 --> 00:35:16,907
{\an8}<i>that people stay at home,
avoid going out at all costs,</i>

618
00:35:17,574 --> 00:35:19,367
<i>regardless of the circumstances.</i>

619
00:35:19,368 --> 00:35:22,787
[reporter] <i>Yes. We'll continue
to monitor and report the situation.</i>

620
00:35:22,788 --> 00:35:24,622
[man on TV] <i>No birds? No iron.</i>

621
00:35:24,623 --> 00:35:27,667
<i>The movement is revolutionary. MOTY.</i>

622
00:35:27,668 --> 00:35:28,669
[sighs]

623
00:35:29,795 --> 00:35:32,421
Private Ra In-ho!
Am I allowed to speak my mind?

624
00:35:32,422 --> 00:35:34,424
Hey, dumbass. Dude, read the room.

625
00:35:35,050 --> 00:35:37,177
What is it? Say it.

626
00:35:39,429 --> 00:35:41,138
There's got to be a reason why yesterday,

627
00:35:41,139 --> 00:35:44,600
Private first class Che Chul-Woo,
didn't actually turn into a zombie

628
00:35:44,601 --> 00:35:45,978
right away after he was bitten.

629
00:35:46,603 --> 00:35:47,687
What do you think it is?

630
00:35:47,688 --> 00:35:50,439
There's a chance it was something
he ate that slowed it down,

631
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:51,441
and that...

632
00:35:57,239 --> 00:35:59,657
I got a feeling
that thing is this ginseng liquid

633
00:35:59,658 --> 00:36:01,200
that Chul-Woo always had on him.

634
00:36:01,201 --> 00:36:04,203
What if this is
what slowed down the infection?

635
00:36:04,204 --> 00:36:05,414
[quirky music playing]

636
00:36:06,999 --> 00:36:07,916
[clicks tongue]

637
00:36:08,834 --> 00:36:10,877
[Gye-young] What
are you talking about, idiot?

638
00:36:10,878 --> 00:36:12,128
Don't just make stuff up.

639
00:36:12,129 --> 00:36:14,214
Private Ra In-ho,
you're incredibly out of line.

640
00:36:14,965 --> 00:36:16,174
[Gye-young] Huh? [gasps]

641
00:36:17,134 --> 00:36:18,009
The way you talk...

642
00:36:18,010 --> 00:36:19,552
What about the way I'm talking?

643
00:36:19,553 --> 00:36:20,888
You talk like a soldier.

644
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:23,098
I'm trying.

645
00:36:23,765 --> 00:36:25,350
So? What?

646
00:36:26,476 --> 00:36:28,269
I have a personal question for you.

647
00:36:28,270 --> 00:36:29,896
Uh, what is it?

648
00:36:29,897 --> 00:36:32,691
How did a civilian like you
learn to shoot that way?

649
00:36:33,233 --> 00:36:35,192
- [Gye-young] Oh...
- Oh...

650
00:36:35,193 --> 00:36:36,527
I was surprised too.

651
00:36:36,528 --> 00:36:38,029
Who taught you to shoot?

652
00:36:38,030 --> 00:36:39,072
Well...

653
00:36:41,283 --> 00:36:43,952
Actually, it's a secret. [chuckles softly]

654
00:36:46,371 --> 00:36:48,998
I was a competitive shooter
until high school.

655
00:36:48,999 --> 00:36:51,126
- National Guard.
- What? Seriously though?

656
00:36:51,752 --> 00:36:54,170
- Wow! Oh, that makes sense.
- [chuckles]

657
00:36:54,171 --> 00:36:55,087
Whoa.

658
00:36:55,088 --> 00:36:56,256
- [gunshot]
- [all gasp]

659
00:36:57,424 --> 00:36:58,758
[intriguing music playing]

660
00:36:58,759 --> 00:36:59,800
What was it?

661
00:36:59,801 --> 00:37:01,219
What was that?

662
00:37:01,929 --> 00:37:04,138
- [Young-man] Shit. Come on.
- [In-ho] Wait for me.

663
00:37:04,139 --> 00:37:06,516
What's going on?

664
00:37:07,601 --> 00:37:08,684
Where was it?

665
00:37:08,685 --> 00:37:09,936
Where'd the shots come from?

666
00:37:09,937 --> 00:37:11,103
The situation room.

667
00:37:11,104 --> 00:37:13,648
- The situation room!
- The Commander?

668
00:37:13,649 --> 00:37:16,276
I think he's held up in the office.

669
00:37:16,860 --> 00:37:18,569
[Gye-young and Jae-yoon gasp]

670
00:37:18,570 --> 00:37:20,656
- Aw, shit.
- Oh, no. [whimpers]

671
00:37:22,658 --> 00:37:24,408
- Let's go. Come on.
- No, wait, wait.

672
00:37:24,409 --> 00:37:25,618
WAR ROOM

673
00:37:25,619 --> 00:37:27,870
[Young-man] Sir, be careful.

674
00:37:27,871 --> 00:37:29,331
[suspenseful music playing]

675
00:37:35,587 --> 00:37:37,172
Shit, why are we doing this?

676
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:40,175
- Wait!
- [In-ho yelps]

677
00:37:41,718 --> 00:37:43,470
[breath trembling]

678
00:37:47,057 --> 00:37:49,392
{\an8}1ST PLATOON DUTY ROSTER

679
00:37:49,393 --> 00:37:51,352
LIVE AS A SHIELD! DIE IN LOYALTY!

680
00:37:51,353 --> 00:37:53,105
[mysterious music playing]

681
00:37:55,440 --> 00:37:57,274
FIRST LIEUTENANT PARK SUNG-WOOK

682
00:37:57,275 --> 00:37:59,319
RETURN TO BRIGADE

683
00:38:12,874 --> 00:38:15,251
[Tripeater] <i>If I manage to get a .209...</i>

684
00:38:15,252 --> 00:38:17,128
- [Young-joo] I got it.
- [Tripeater] You did?

685
00:38:17,129 --> 00:38:18,713
- ...209?
- [Young-joo] I got it.

686
00:38:18,714 --> 00:38:20,214
- I got it.
- [Tripeater] You sure?

687
00:38:20,215 --> 00:38:22,174
- You got it.
- [Young-joo cheering]

688
00:38:22,175 --> 00:38:24,051
- You got it. You got it.
- [laughing]

689
00:38:24,052 --> 00:38:27,096
- [Young-joo] I got it.
- [Tripeater] You got it. You got it.

690
00:38:27,097 --> 00:38:29,265
- [Young-joo] Amazing.
- [Tripeater] Well done.

691
00:38:29,266 --> 00:38:31,434
- Wow, I feel great.
- [Young-joo groans]

692
00:38:31,435 --> 00:38:33,144
I'm so drunk. Wasted...

693
00:38:33,145 --> 00:38:34,353
Completely shitfaced.

694
00:38:34,354 --> 00:38:35,479
[Young-joo groans]

695
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:36,398
[sighs]

696
00:38:38,275 --> 00:38:39,234
[drunkenly] Idiot.

697
00:38:39,735 --> 00:38:40,735
Ah...

698
00:38:40,736 --> 00:38:43,571
So you pretended to be
strong and independent,

699
00:38:43,572 --> 00:38:45,781
but you can't keep up with us. [chuckles]

700
00:38:45,782 --> 00:38:47,533
[Tripeater] Can you untie me, please?

701
00:38:47,534 --> 00:38:51,955
I have the highest blood alcohol level
out of all of you. [hiccups]

702
00:38:52,539 --> 00:38:54,540
- Should I?
- Absolutely not.

703
00:38:54,541 --> 00:38:56,375
- We can't.
- I'm sorry, bro.

704
00:38:56,376 --> 00:38:59,045
When in the hell will you untie him?

705
00:38:59,046 --> 00:39:01,672
Just... The sun's already up.

706
00:39:01,673 --> 00:39:03,090
If we get drunk like this,

707
00:39:03,091 --> 00:39:06,260
won't it be harder
to deal with the zombies?

708
00:39:06,261 --> 00:39:07,970
Hey, nothing's easy.

709
00:39:07,971 --> 00:39:09,096
[Tae-shik] Young-joo.

710
00:39:09,097 --> 00:39:10,598
Our goal is Tower A.

711
00:39:10,599 --> 00:39:11,807
We're going.

712
00:39:11,808 --> 00:39:14,351
Why in the hell are you going to Tower A?

713
00:39:14,352 --> 00:39:16,646
- What's your boyfriend got to do with it?
- Hey!

714
00:39:17,272 --> 00:39:20,524
- Do you want to repeat a fourth time?
- Young-joo! [hiccups]

715
00:39:20,525 --> 00:39:21,526
Look...

716
00:39:22,486 --> 00:39:24,529
all of us have to go over to Tower A,

717
00:39:25,155 --> 00:39:27,782
so we can meet up
with the soldiers and be safer.

718
00:39:27,783 --> 00:39:29,200
And be with Jae-yoon.

719
00:39:29,201 --> 00:39:31,786
Correct.
And your Private Jae-yoon is there.

720
00:39:31,787 --> 00:39:32,870
He'll save us.

721
00:39:32,871 --> 00:39:35,122
I got a car too, and it's an American car.

722
00:39:35,123 --> 00:39:36,207
- American car?
- Oh...

723
00:39:36,208 --> 00:39:38,292
- [Tae-shik] Yes.
- American cars are awesome.

724
00:39:38,293 --> 00:39:40,002
The survival kit's there too.

725
00:39:40,003 --> 00:39:41,796
- Where are you going?
- Can you untie me?

726
00:39:41,797 --> 00:39:42,963
[Young-joo chuckles]

727
00:39:42,964 --> 00:39:44,340
[Tae-shik] You're too wasted.

728
00:39:44,341 --> 00:39:45,883
- Let's go.
- Where are you...

729
00:39:45,884 --> 00:39:48,720
Hey, Kang Young-joo. Wait up.
Kang Young-joo!

730
00:39:49,429 --> 00:39:51,180
Hey, where you going, dude?

731
00:39:51,181 --> 00:39:53,224
- Come back! Hey!
- [Young-joo] I'm free!

732
00:39:53,225 --> 00:39:55,267
[Tae-shik singing] <i>I've got a hammer...</i>

733
00:39:55,268 --> 00:39:56,519
[Jin-wook] Kang Young-joo.

734
00:39:56,520 --> 00:39:59,688
[singing] <i>Brother, I'm sorry
I can't untie those hands</i>

735
00:39:59,689 --> 00:40:01,108
<i>My car is off-road</i>

736
00:40:01,733 --> 00:40:03,109
<i>And it is safe</i>

737
00:40:03,110 --> 00:40:04,194
<i>It's very safe</i>

738
00:40:06,822 --> 00:40:07,863
Where'd they go?

739
00:40:07,864 --> 00:40:09,699
[solemn music playing]

740
00:40:15,664 --> 00:40:16,873
[Jae-yoon] I think it's over.

741
00:40:18,458 --> 00:40:19,291
[In-ho] Huh?

742
00:40:19,292 --> 00:40:21,795
[sighs] There's no reason
for us to be here.

743
00:40:22,963 --> 00:40:24,047
I don't understand. What?

744
00:40:24,965 --> 00:40:27,217
Our service here has no use any longer.

745
00:40:30,595 --> 00:40:31,930
Jae-yoon, wait. Are you...

746
00:40:32,848 --> 00:40:36,560
going to desert us
and go try to find your girlfriend?

747
00:40:40,397 --> 00:40:42,106
Yeah. How am I supposed to just wait here

748
00:40:42,107 --> 00:40:45,360
when she could've gotten hurt
on her way to see me at the tower?

749
00:40:46,111 --> 00:40:47,820
- [sighs]
- [In-ho clears throat]

750
00:40:47,821 --> 00:40:50,866
I need to find Young-joo.
I have to get out of here now.

751
00:40:52,033 --> 00:40:52,868
[grunts]

752
00:40:54,327 --> 00:40:56,288
Then I'll go along with you.

753
00:40:58,915 --> 00:41:00,541
And we'll leave together.

754
00:41:00,542 --> 00:41:03,170
I have got to protect Hayul and my wife!

755
00:41:03,879 --> 00:41:04,713
Yeah.

756
00:41:05,672 --> 00:41:06,506
Yeah.

757
00:41:07,215 --> 00:41:09,551
We have got to be sure
our loved ones are safe.

758
00:41:12,220 --> 00:41:13,513
[sighs] Let's go.

759
00:41:15,056 --> 00:41:16,765
Let's go speak with the Commander.

760
00:41:16,766 --> 00:41:17,851
[In-ho] Hmm?

761
00:41:19,144 --> 00:41:20,312
Wait, right now?

762
00:41:23,190 --> 00:41:24,565
[zombies growling]

763
00:41:24,566 --> 00:41:25,941
[Young-joo] Ah, zombies!

764
00:41:25,942 --> 00:41:27,693
- Move out of the way.
- [zombies growling]

765
00:41:27,694 --> 00:41:30,946
- I have to go and see Jae-yoon!
- Hey, are you crazy? Shh!

766
00:41:30,947 --> 00:41:32,323
[Young-joo] Ugh...

767
00:41:32,324 --> 00:41:34,950
I thought you said
zombies can't attack when you're drunk.

768
00:41:34,951 --> 00:41:35,910
- Let's go.
- [groans]

769
00:41:35,911 --> 00:41:38,120
- Come here. Come on.
- [Young-joo groans]

770
00:41:38,121 --> 00:41:39,747
[zombies growling]

771
00:41:39,748 --> 00:41:41,249
- [Jin-wook] Come on.
- [gasps]

772
00:41:43,376 --> 00:41:46,420
- [Jin-wook] This way. Oh, wait, wait.
- [Young-joo groans]

773
00:41:46,421 --> 00:41:48,505
- Hey, zombies!
- [Jin-wook] Hey, stop.

774
00:41:48,506 --> 00:41:51,175
- Hey, come here. Hey!
- Come on, please, let's go.

775
00:41:51,176 --> 00:41:53,719
- I can totally win again them.
- No, you can't win.

776
00:41:53,720 --> 00:41:54,637
You will never win.

777
00:41:54,638 --> 00:41:56,305
[Young-joo groans]

778
00:41:56,306 --> 00:41:58,140
[panting]

779
00:41:58,141 --> 00:42:00,059
[Jin-wook] Oh, fuck, we're fucked!

780
00:42:00,060 --> 00:42:02,728
Fuck, we can't run away now.
We're gonna get eaten!

781
00:42:02,729 --> 00:42:04,521
[Jin-wook sobbing]

782
00:42:04,522 --> 00:42:05,732
[laughing]

783
00:42:07,692 --> 00:42:08,817
Is that funny? Huh?

784
00:42:08,818 --> 00:42:09,902
[laughing]

785
00:42:09,903 --> 00:42:11,154
[Tripeater laughing]

786
00:42:11,947 --> 00:42:13,113
Oh, gosh.

787
00:42:13,114 --> 00:42:14,823
What the hell? You got scared?

788
00:42:14,824 --> 00:42:17,868
Hey, you said
they can't actually bite you, right?

789
00:42:17,869 --> 00:42:19,411
Go and do something about it.

790
00:42:19,412 --> 00:42:21,372
Then go ahead and untie me, dude.

791
00:42:21,373 --> 00:42:23,415
Are you seriously
asking that right now?

792
00:42:23,416 --> 00:42:25,084
- Hey, untie him, now!
- [groans]

793
00:42:25,085 --> 00:42:26,919
- Okay.
- You can just do it yourself.

794
00:42:26,920 --> 00:42:29,213
I can't help all tied up like this.

795
00:42:29,214 --> 00:42:31,048
- [sighs]
- Okay, I'll untie you.

796
00:42:31,049 --> 00:42:32,508
Untie him. [laughing]

797
00:42:32,509 --> 00:42:34,176
[Jin-wook] Here. It's off.

798
00:42:34,177 --> 00:42:36,553
- [Young-joo] It's done. Yeah.
- [sighs]

799
00:42:36,554 --> 00:42:37,471
[growls]

800
00:42:37,472 --> 00:42:39,014
[both gasp]

801
00:42:39,015 --> 00:42:40,767
[Young-joo and Tripeater laugh]

802
00:42:42,102 --> 00:42:44,478
- Go, go.
- I trust you.

803
00:42:44,479 --> 00:42:45,813
[quirky music playing]

804
00:42:45,814 --> 00:42:48,191
[zombies growling]

805
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:55,239
- [Young-joo groans] I don't feel good.
- Shh!

806
00:42:55,240 --> 00:42:57,574
[zombies growling]

807
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:58,492
[horn honks]

808
00:42:58,493 --> 00:42:59,535
[mumbling]

809
00:42:59,536 --> 00:43:01,245
[horn honking]

810
00:43:01,246 --> 00:43:02,747
[zombies growling]

811
00:43:09,004 --> 00:43:11,755
- [Jin-wook] Hey, hey. Get up.
- [Young-joo] Where are we going?

812
00:43:11,756 --> 00:43:13,675
- [horn honking]
- [zombies growling]

813
00:43:16,428 --> 00:43:18,847
- [Tripeater] Wait for me!
- [Young-joo] Hey, you!

814
00:43:19,556 --> 00:43:21,725
- [Tripeater] Woo-hoo!
- [Young-joo] Hurry up!

815
00:43:25,061 --> 00:43:26,813
[solemn music playing]

816
00:43:31,568 --> 00:43:33,862
CHOI CHUL-WOO - PARK SUNG-WOOK
JEON HYUNG-BAE

817
00:43:36,364 --> 00:43:37,574
SAFETY
FIRE

818
00:43:43,121 --> 00:43:44,539
[breath trembling]

819
00:43:45,248 --> 00:43:46,708
[sniffles and sighs]

820
00:43:49,002 --> 00:43:50,378
[whimpering]

821
00:43:51,963 --> 00:43:53,256
[sobbing]

822
00:43:59,095 --> 00:43:59,971
[sighs]

823
00:44:04,184 --> 00:44:06,602
[Jae-yoon] Privates Lee Jae-yoon
and Ra In-ho. Sir, we'd--

824
00:44:06,603 --> 00:44:07,812
Oh...

825
00:44:10,273 --> 00:44:11,107
[gulps]

826
00:44:13,151 --> 00:44:14,568
Yeah. What's going on?

827
00:44:14,569 --> 00:44:15,903
What is...

828
00:44:15,904 --> 00:44:17,072
going on?

829
00:44:17,655 --> 00:44:18,740
Uh, yeah.

830
00:44:19,657 --> 00:44:21,368
Park Sung-wook. Um...

831
00:44:22,494 --> 00:44:24,244
I was trying to... [sniffles]

832
00:44:24,245 --> 00:44:26,663
Ballistics... Like... like this.

833
00:44:26,664 --> 00:44:28,832
Like... like... like this... direction.

834
00:44:28,833 --> 00:44:30,667
- Inspection.
- Inspection?

835
00:44:30,668 --> 00:44:32,670
- Yes, that's right.
- [both] Oh.

836
00:44:33,838 --> 00:44:34,839
Inspection.

837
00:44:35,590 --> 00:44:38,634
I was conducting
an inspection on Park's case.

838
00:44:38,635 --> 00:44:39,676
Why are you here?

839
00:44:39,677 --> 00:44:43,305
Oh. Yes, sir. We're really low on food,
and our current issue is figuring out

840
00:44:43,306 --> 00:44:45,641
how to successfully access
our resupply lines.

841
00:44:45,642 --> 00:44:47,893
Sadly, we've got
an even bigger problem on our hands.

842
00:44:47,894 --> 00:44:50,187
- Which is?
- Private In-ho, explain it to him.

843
00:44:50,188 --> 00:44:52,232
Private Ra In-ho. Allow me to explain!

844
00:44:52,732 --> 00:44:56,026
As you recall yesterday,
the power went out, then turned back on,

845
00:44:56,027 --> 00:44:58,445
and without having any power,
we had no ATS.

846
00:44:58,446 --> 00:44:59,906
Yeah, I remember yesterday.

847
00:45:00,698 --> 00:45:02,950
At that point,
the hotel's electricity supply

848
00:45:02,951 --> 00:45:05,744
should have switched over
from external to the backups.

849
00:45:05,745 --> 00:45:07,996
Which means the only reason
that we have water

850
00:45:07,997 --> 00:45:09,832
is because the water tanks are running.

851
00:45:09,833 --> 00:45:13,377
So the tanks, the water and the pumps
are currently only being powered

852
00:45:13,378 --> 00:45:15,712
solely by the hotel's generators.

853
00:45:15,713 --> 00:45:17,173
If the generators give out,

854
00:45:17,715 --> 00:45:19,717
then our water supply will also run out.

855
00:45:22,846 --> 00:45:24,431
When do you think that will be?

856
00:45:25,640 --> 00:45:27,350
[gulps] I would say...

857
00:45:28,017 --> 00:45:29,727
we only have a few days remaining.

858
00:45:30,437 --> 00:45:31,270
That's all.

859
00:45:31,271 --> 00:45:32,605
[quirky music playing]

860
00:45:37,402 --> 00:45:38,653
[phone ringing]

861
00:45:41,531 --> 00:45:43,490
This is Master Sergeant Jung speaking.

862
00:45:43,491 --> 00:45:45,868
- [man] <i>This is Battalion commander.</i>
- Salute.

863
00:45:45,869 --> 00:45:48,620
[man] <i>I'm sending
a resupply helicopter by noon today.</i>

864
00:45:48,621 --> 00:45:50,914
<i>Make sure to meet us
on the roof right on arrival.</i>

865
00:45:50,915 --> 00:45:52,249
<i>- Stand by.</i>
- Yes.

866
00:45:52,250 --> 00:45:53,500
[drums beating]

867
00:45:53,501 --> 00:45:56,503
At noon,
the supply helicopter will arrive.

868
00:45:56,504 --> 00:45:57,797
- What?
- [Soo-jeong] Hmm?

869
00:45:58,298 --> 00:46:00,799
[Tae-hwa] The first time
we've had a heli in the compound,

870
00:46:00,800 --> 00:46:02,468
but if we stay on top of it,

871
00:46:02,469 --> 00:46:04,344
- we should be able to handle it.
- Shit, man.

872
00:46:04,345 --> 00:46:06,263
[Tae-hwa] Remember safety first.

873
00:46:06,264 --> 00:46:08,056
Everybody remain alert.

874
00:46:08,057 --> 00:46:09,183
Be ready for anything.

875
00:46:09,184 --> 00:46:10,935
- All right?
- [all] Yes, sir

876
00:46:11,728 --> 00:46:14,480
[Tae-hwa] From now on,
leave your armor on at all times.

877
00:46:14,481 --> 00:46:17,900
Gye-young, go get some more armor.
Soo-Jeong should wear it as well.

878
00:46:17,901 --> 00:46:19,568
Yes, sir!

879
00:46:19,569 --> 00:46:20,694
Thank you, sir!

880
00:46:20,695 --> 00:46:22,280
[sighs and grunts]

881
00:46:23,072 --> 00:46:23,948
[chuckles]

882
00:46:25,575 --> 00:46:27,285
[sighs and groans]

883
00:46:30,497 --> 00:46:32,040
[military music playing]

884
00:46:36,377 --> 00:46:39,589
[soldier] Opera, this is Eagle One.
Approaching the rooftop now.

885
00:46:41,716 --> 00:46:43,009
[helicopter hovering]

886
00:46:44,260 --> 00:46:45,303
<i>Bringing her down.</i>

887
00:46:47,805 --> 00:46:49,848
[Gye-young] Oh, come on. Hurry up.

888
00:46:49,849 --> 00:46:51,725
[Soo-jeong] It's coming. It's coming.

889
00:46:51,726 --> 00:46:54,102
[Kyung-sik] This is Opera, Opera.
Fish, respond.

890
00:46:54,103 --> 00:46:55,939
Can't that thing just take me home?

891
00:46:57,649 --> 00:46:59,608
- They can do that?
- [Gye-young] Should I ask?

892
00:46:59,609 --> 00:47:02,237
This is Opera, Opera. Fish, respond.

893
00:47:14,249 --> 00:47:16,084
[somber music playing]

